gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.02950479648670501,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.18640701335207766,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.005198265280877521,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":55.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0315288972383192,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":46.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.022955529419399934,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":78.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0016619326766181182,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0021600001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.1,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":10.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Phillips 66 operates as an integrated downstream energy provider in the United States, the United Kingdom, Germany, and internationally. It operates through five segments: Midstream, Chemicals, Refining, Marketing and Specialties (M&S), and Renewable Fuels. The Midstream segment provides crude oil and refined petroleum product transportation, terminaling, and storage services, as well as natural gas and natural gas liquids (NGL) gathering, processing, transportation, fractionation, storage and marketing services. It also exports liquefied petroleum gas. The Chemicals segment produces and markets ethylene and other olefin products; aromatics and styrenics products, such as benzene, cyclohexane, styrene, and polystyrene; various specialty chemical products, including organosulfur chemicals, solvents, catalysts, and chemicals used in drilling and mining; and petrochemicals and plastics. The Refining segment refines crude oil and other feedstocks into petroleum products, such as gasolines and distillates, including aviation fuels. The M&S segment purchases for resale and markets refined products, including gasolines, distillates, and aviation fuels. This segment also manufactures and markets specialty products, such as automotive, commercial, industrial, and specialty lubricants, as well as base oils. The Renewable Fuels segment processes renewable feedstocks into renewable products, as well as supplies sustainable aviation fuel. This segment also procures renewable feedstocks, manages certain regulatory credits, and markets renewable diesel, renewable jet fuel, and other renewable fuels. The company markets its products under the Phillips 66, Conoco and 76, JET, Kendall, Red Line, and other private label brands. Phillips 66 was founded in 1875 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Mark E. Lashier | CEO & Chairman | Age 63 | Compensation: $6.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $10.5M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Phillips 66 is a large-cap energy business with a $95.8B market cap on $132.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 6.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 104% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0352389937948427},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (90% sell ratio, net $7473.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Phillips 66 (NYSE:PSX) Stock Price Down 1.2% \u2013 Should You Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/phillips-66-nysepsx-stock-price-down-1-2-should-you-sell.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793936514.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Phillips 66 (PSX) Secures Long Term Used Cooking Oil Supply For Renewable Fuels","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/phillips-66-psx-secures-long-170952479.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793812192.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Phillips 66 (PSX) Posts Strong Q3 Results, Is The Upside Fully Priced?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-psx/phillips-66/news/phillips-66-psx-posts-strong-q3-results-is-the-upside-fully","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793794615.851,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.842,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Phillips 66 Stock Worth Buying Despite Its Premium Valuation?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025649/is-phillips-66-stock-worth-buying-despite-its-premium-valuation?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cmost_popular_stocks-3025649","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793975580.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Zacks Analyst Blog Highlights Phillips 66, Valero Energy and HF Sinclair","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3022460/the-zacks-analyst-blog-highlights-phillips-66-valero-energy-and-hf-sinclair?cid=CS-ZC-FT-press_releases-3022460","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793776560.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can MPC's Gulf Coast Focus Fuel Stronger Future Refining Returns?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/new